{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug final report for the patchset-1 CI failure. Problem: Gerrit Verified run 31152961333 failed every lock-installing job before tests. Proven root cause: pyproject.toml bumped the root project to 0.11.0 while uv.lock retained `name = \"nava-rebar\"`, `version = \"0.10.1\"`; the release plan omitted uv.lock. Proof: CI `uv sync --locked --extra dev` and local held-out `uv lock --check` emitted the same stale-lock error. Test: held-out `uv lock --check` was RED before repair, GREEN after regeneration, returned RED again when the exact stale root version was mutation-restored, and returned GREEN after restoring the fix. Fix: canonical lock regeneration changed exactly one field, root version 0.10.1 -> 0.11.0; no dependency name/version/hash changed. `uv sync --locked --extra dev --dry-run` would make no changes. Scope/safety: ticket description, file impact, and ACs now include uv.lock; amended plan review is certified; no dependency, API, runtime, security, or performance behavior was added. Siblings: none—this is the single root-project entry in the lock. Replication: the original locked sync passed in the fixer run. The release commit was amended and explicitly rebased onto current origin/main bfdb68070a; focused upstream tests 4 passed, release guards 36 passed, lint/typecheck passed, rebuilt wheel/sdist passed Twine. Final rebased artifact hashes: sdist 9efdf3623ab31bdd2be4ccb74b729101955d023f66f54610399d0945f8b8ffcb; wheel f117ac931a5ce4bdf36e9a5f92174a3f72067b02d63eb4915ff7fee88884eceb."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786083789474116001,"uuid":"4607eff5-d2a3-4617-b818-86cce312068f"}